vity  sucks you generally took very little  full damage in Demon Souls but at a  certain point drop damage just increases  exponentially and your knees just  exploded past this point but beyond this  how much the gameplay changes would  depend on how much from software is  involved and there is a lot they could  change if they had a mind to I would say  the first thing that comes to mind is  omnidirectional rolling since in the  original you could only really roll in a  few directions while you were locked on  that's probably the single biggest thing  they could do to make the game feel  modern and in line with recent titles  next magic is just way too overpowered  in demon souls while I love that magic  in this game can be cast more freely and  I also prefer how you can get mana to  regenerate and I prefer how it's used as  a resource but  the royalty starting class which starts  with magic just puts you on such a  pedestal compared to the other classes  and you carry that advantage with you  through the entire game right up until  the last boss another poorly balanced  thing about Demon Souls is the healing  system so in this game you heal by  consuming grass and there are different  types of grafts that all heal different  amounts it's kind of like blood-borne in  the sense that you have to farm for your  healing items but it's also more extreme  than blood-borne because you can carry  more than 20 healing items and some of  those healing items heal your full  health bar so if you want to you can  just farm powerful healing items and  abuse the hell out of them which is also  a really bad problem in PvP something  like Estus would be so much better but  the most controversial mechanic in Demon  Souls was something called world  tendency and for those who don't know  this was a mechanic whereby the world  itself would respond to your deaths and  also to the deaths of players around you  if you're playing offline then your  world tendency starts at neutral and it  