me people are  taking the snowy scene in the remake  trailer as proof that we'll be exploring  this area I do want to remind you guys  that a snowy scene was seen in the  original prologue as well in a week or  so I'll actually have a video going far  more in depth on the broken arch stone  and the land of the giants that  supposedly lies beyond it so subscribe  for that turn on notifications because  we actually know a lot more about the  lore of this place than most people  think and I'm excited to share some new  discoveries with you all funnily enough  the world that you saw in our painted  world poster was actually meant to  depict the land of the giants and also  the broken arch stone so if you  purchased this poster or you want to go  and take a closer look link in the  description of course a new area to  explore would mean new items weapons  armors and demon souls could actually do  with a lot more of these because the  original selection is quite limited so I  can think of two big questions that  remain first what is or what was  fracture  mode is at what I mentioned earlier  where you might be able to revert the  game back to its original graphics or  does it have to do with gameplay or  demon souls actually originally had a  permadeath mode before it was removed  maybe it's that but I'd love to hear  your thoughts in the comments on what  fractured mode could be and lastly a  release date I have a bit of a theory on  this so there isn't a release date  currently and you know what else doesn't  have a release date PlayStation 5  therefore I think it's possible that  Demon Souls could be a PS 5 launch title  which would explain why they haven't  mentioned anything the other alternative  is that the game still has a bit more  development to go so maybe it's gonna be  released next year who knows regardless  I'm so excited for this game eight  months ago I made a video on why I  thought Demon Souls deserves a remaster  so go and watch that if you want to know  what made this game so special Demon  Souls just took so many risks as a game  and it's incredibly close to my heart  and it's about time the newer members of  the souls community played this game  because I know like 75% of you haven't  which is a huge shame but I'm excited  for you guys so thank you so much for  watching and see you in the next video  where I actually plan to announce the  next art competition guess what it's  about I shall await then return slayer  of demons I am here for thee in the only  [Music]
 

